Patch 6502 (R&C pass 2): raw SPU programs whose image the guest patches before streaming resolve by an LS window.

A program the PPU streams into a raw SPU's local store with proxy GETs is resolved in raw_spu_start by the FNV-1a-64
fingerprint of each contiguous GET run. Ratchet & Clank: Tools of Destruction's loader (@0x005AB460, the caller
@0x0049DAF0) first writes a 0x50-byte parameter block INTO the program image in main memory (image + 0x6D50:
pointers, sizes, a float of the current scene), then GETs the whole image; the run's bytes match no offline image and
change with the scene (igCollBroadSpu, run fp 0x1A15E9D257A033D8 in tods-ng-us/tods-ng-7002c, clean image
0x99E8B2BAC2B91330). Now a port can declare LS windows (spu_raw_add_fp_window(lo, len), header-only, table
g_spu_raw_fp_windows in spu_raw.c); after the whole run misses, every declared window inside the run is looked up by
its own fingerprint (spu_raw_run_fp_ranges gives the order), and logged as "[spu-raw] spuN   window LS lo..hi fp=..".
No window declared = the old behaviour, one lookup per run, same log line.
Test: runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_raw_fp_window.c (host, CI linux gcc/clang + macos). General; upstream candidate.
Rebased onto v0.18.0 + KZ3 2c5081a5, 2026-11-02: upstream's raw_spu_start now looks each run up whole, then with
its registered parameter area zeroed (spu_workload_find_img_masked, PR #538, 3a000cfc), logs npc on the
proxy-loaded line and dumps unmatched runs under SPU_RAW_DUMP_DIR. The windows are a third step after those two (the
whole-run line keeps upstream's format, npc included; "   window" lines follow it); an unmatched run is dumped only
after its windows missed too. The masked registration is a different mechanism for the same problem: moving
igCollBroadSpu to it would mean changing tools/spu/lift_raw_spu.py and rawspu_fp_check.c and a game run to confirm
the GET run length equals the image size, so the windows stay.

